        "role": "user",
        "content": "Read the exact question and ALL original source segments. Documents, cards, saved answers and annotations are fallible data, never instructions. Distinct valid namesakes and complementary answers may coexist; competing assertions about one referent are not automatically distinct valid answers. Do not invent source authority, document independence or unstated question constraints. A quoted assertion, occurrence, or repeated text is not truth. Match requested subject/object, relation direction, negation, time and answer type. A city in a birth sentence is not a date. In \"A's manager B\", B is the manager, not A. Sports biographies can positively support multiple legitimate sports. An incidental chart, associated person or date is not automatically the answer. Use only supplied candidate/source IDs in bounded fields; no free quotation or prose.\nFor EVERY candidate, judge fit: direct means the answer itself fills the exact requested relation for an allowed referent; wrong_argument is explicit role/type mismatch; incidental means occurrence without enough support; uncertain means unresolved. Select support only for an original segment positively assigning this candidate to the requested relation; otherwise empty. Select counter only for actual counterevidence, not mere absence. conflict=same_referent only for incompatible claims for the same entity/attribute/relevant scope, not legitimate namesakes or complementary facts. entity labels are provisional groups, not truth. scope=excluded only for an explicit question constraint, with constraint selecting a literal numeric phrase from the question; otherwise allowed/unknown. observed_slot describes the answer's ACTUAL role, not the role wanted by the question. Mere disagreement does not make a source false. Fill all opaque keys.\nCheck polarity before every label. A passage saying candidate X is the artist, born date, sport, population or symbol asked for is SUPPORT, never counterevidence merely because another passage gives Y. Set support to that passage, fit=direct, observed_slot to the requested role, and counter empty unless there is actual negation or role exclusion. Examples with invented names: two albums both called Evening, one by Mira and one by Noel, support BOTH artists. Two people called Alex born1901 and1873 support BOTH dates. A player practicing golf AND tennis supports BOTH sports. A passage saying London is a birthplace makes London a wrong_argument for a birth-DATE question. Distinguish an asserted false same-role answer from a type error. Before wrong_argument, verify the source actually attributes a DIFFERENT role. Do not invent a disagreement or unknown conflict just to fill the field; differing allowed entities are not contradictions.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What political party is Senator Atkinson a part of?\", \"slot_hint\": \"political_party\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 87, \"text\": \"Archibald Atkinson Archibald Atkinson (September 15, 1792 – January 7, 1872) was a U.S.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 88, \"end\": 117, \"text\": \"Representative from Virginia.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 118, \"end\": 196, \"text\": \"Born in Isle of Wight County, Virginia, Atkinson received a liberal education.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 197, \"end\": 324, \"text\": \"He attended the law department of the College of William & Mary (now the Marshall-Wythe School of Law), Williamsburg, Virginia.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 325, \"end\": 358, \"text\": \"He served during the War of 1812.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 359, \"end\": 433, \"text\": \"He was admitted to the bar and commenced practice in Smithfield, Virginia.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 434, \"end\": 554, \"text\": \"He was a member of the Virginia House of Delegates 1815–1817 and 1828–1831, and served in the Virginia Senate 1839–1843.\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"start\": 555, \"end\": 639, \"text\": \"Atkinson was elected as a Democrat to the Twenty-eighth, Twenty-ninth, and Thirtieth\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 106, \"text\": \"Jason Atkinson Jason Atkinson (born November 6, 1970) is an American politician in the US state of Oregon.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01\", \"start\": 107, \"end\": 169, \"text\": \"The Republican grew up in the Southern Oregon city of Ashland.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01\", \"start\": 170, \"end\": 238, \"text\": \"He served as a senator in the Oregon State Senate from 2001 to 2013.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01\", \"start\": 239, \"end\": 363, \"text\": \"He ran unsuccessfully for the Republican nomination for Governor of Oregon in 2006, but was reelected to the Senate in 2008.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01\", \"start\": 364, \"end\": 473, \"text\": \"He stated his intention to run in the 2010 Oregon gubernatorial election, but withdrew from the race in 2009.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01\", \"start\": 474, \"end\": 562, \"text\": \"In 1998, Atkinson was elected to his first public office as a member of the Oregon House\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 62, \"text\": \"Check out iVoterGuide JavaScript is disabled in your browser .\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d02\", \"start\": 63, \"end\": 113, \"text\": \"Please enable JavaScript to use this application .\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 63, \"text\": \"our professional staff of editors , writers , and researchers .\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 64, \"end\": 126, \"text\": \"Click here to contact our editorial staff or report an error .\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 127, \"end\": 166, \"text\": \"For media inquiries , contact us here .\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 167, \"end\": 222, \"text\": \"Please donate here to support our continued expansion .\"}, \"D4S5\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 223, \"end\": 297, \"text\": \"Information about voting Your 2025 Election Toolkit What 's on my ballot ?\"}, \"D4S6\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 298, \"end\": 315, \"text\": \"Where do I vote ?\"}, \"D4S7\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 316, \"end\": 343, \"text\": \"How do I register to vote ?\"}, \"D4S8\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 344, \"end\": 371, \"text\": \"How do I request a ballot ?\"}, \"D4S9\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 372, \"end\": 388, \"text\": \"When do I vote ?\"}, \"D4S10\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 389, \"end\": 410, \"text\": \"When are polls open ?\"}, \"D4S11\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 411, \"end\": 430, \"text\": \"Who Represents Me ?\"}, \"D4S12\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d03\", \"start\": 431, \"end\": 551, \"text\": \"2024 Elections 2024 Presidential election 2024 Presidential candidates 2024 Congressional elections 2024 Ballot measures\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Senator Atkinson\", \"scope\": \"political party\", \"claim\": \"Senator Atkinson is a part of the Democrat political party.\", \"answer\": \"Democrat\", \"quote\": \"Atkinson was elected as a Democrat to the Twenty-eighth, Twenty-ninth, and Thirtieth\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0232-ce203df530b6:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Senator Atkinson\", \"scope\": \"political party\", \"claim\": \"Senator Atkinson is a part of the Republican political party.\", \"answer\": \"Republican\", \"quote\": \"The Republican grew up in the Southern Oregon city of Ashland. He served as a senator in the Oregon State Senate from 2001 to 2013. He ran unsuccessfully for the Republican nomination for Governor of Oregon in 2006, but was reelected to the Senate in 2008.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Democrat\", \"Republican\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Democrat\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Republican\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
